%[text] %[text:anchor:T_CFF3DFB5] # Air Track Collisions Lab: Virtual Experiment
%[text] [⇦ Return to the main menu](<matlab: open(fullfile(currentProject().RootFolder,'MainMenu.m'))>)
%%
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_8AA5F0BC] ### **Explore the virtual experimental setup**
%[text] 1. Open the Simscape Multibody model: [airTrackLab](<matlab:  airTrackLab>)
%[text] 2. Run the model ![Run button](text:image:1e41) and observe it in the Mechanics Explorer.
%[text] 3. Adjust the windows so that the Mechanics Explorer is alongside the Simulink window.
%[text] 4. Use the controls to push the carts. You should push the carts while the model is still running.
%[text] 5. When you push a cart and it passes through the photogate, the duration of time that the cart's presence is detected by the sensor is recorded in the readout. Try pushing the cart harder by holding the push button longer.
%[text] 6. Stop ![Stop button](text:image:8b98) the simulation to reset it.
%[text] 7. Adjust the starting positions and weights by double-clicking the air track model labeled: "Double click here to adjust the starting positions and weights." Rerun the model and observe the changes in the behavior.
%[text] 8. Review the simulation by adjusting the slider at the bottom of the Mechanics Explorer window: ![Time slider](text:image:388e) \
%[text]{"align":"center"} ![How to use the Simscape Multibody air track model](text:image:9abf)
%[text]{"align":"center"} *How to use the Simscape Multibody air track model*
%%
